          %h1#sublocales Sublocales
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_regular_monomorphisms_of_locales"} In terms of regular monomorphisms of locales
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_subsets_of_opens"} In terms of subsets of opens
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#equivalence_of_these_two_definitions"} Equivalence of these two definitions
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_nuclei"} In terms of nuclei
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#equivalence_of_nuclei_and_other_definitions"} Equivalence of nuclei and other definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#special_cases"} Special cases
              %li
                %a{:href => "#relation_to_topological_subspaces"} Relation to topological subspaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A sublocale is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            It is important to understand that, even for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (which can be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are
            %em not
            topological. Specifically, we have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inclusion+function"} inclusion function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Sub
                  %mi Loc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub Top(X) \hookrightarrow Sub Loc(X)
            which, while
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjective
          %p
            Sublocales can also be defined for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+topologies"} formal topologies
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p There are multiple equivalent ways to formally define this concept.
          %h3#in_terms_of_regular_monomorphisms_of_locales In terms of regular monomorphisms of locales
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
          %p
            A
            %strong sublocale
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+subobject"} regular subobject
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loc"} Loc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of locales. Equivalently, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+quotient"} regular quotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frm"} Frm
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
          %p
            Equivalently, a sublocale of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            can be described as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\to S
            whose underlying map of sets is surjective.
          %h3#in_terms_of_subsets_of_opens In terms of subsets of opens
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular monomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon S\to L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\dashv f_*
            between the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*: S\to L
          %p
            is an injection on underlying sets such that if we equip its image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(S)
            with the induced order, it becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            itself, and the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(S)\to L
            is a localic map, i.e., it has a left adjoint that preserves finite meets.
          %p
            Thus, sublocales of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            can be defined as subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            once we equip it with the order induced from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\to L
            exists and preserves finite meets. (Proposition 2.2 in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#PicadoPultr12"} Picado &amp; Pultr 2012
          %p
            (The inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\to L
            need not preserve joins, so in particular, the lattice structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            may be different from that of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            Equivalently, sublocales of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            can also be described (
            %a{:href => "#PicadoPultr12"}> PP12 §2.1
            ) as subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            that are closed under all meets and for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in S
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in L
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x\to s)\in S
          %h3#equivalence_of_these_two_definitions Equivalence of these two definitions
          %p
            Given a surjective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon L\to S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_*(S)
            is a sublocale of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            Given a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of a locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            that is a sublocale, the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*\colon L\to S
            to the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_*\colon S\to L
            is a surjective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
          %h3#in_terms_of_nuclei In terms of nuclei
          %p
            A sublocale is given precisely by a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleus"} nucleus
            on the underlying frame. This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            from the opens of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to the opens of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            satisfying the following identities:
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(U \cap V) = j(U) \cap j(V)
              ,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq j(U)
              ,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(j(U)) = j(U)
              \.
          %p
            In other words, a sublocale of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is given by a
            = succeed "-preserving" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on its frame of opens.
          %p
            The precise reasons why nuclei correspond to quotient frames (and hence to sublocales) is given at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleus"} nucleus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is this: we identify two opens if they ‘agree on the sublocale’. Given an open
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %h3#equivalence_of_nuclei_and_other_definitions Equivalence of nuclei and other definitions
          %p
            Given a nucleus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            given by the equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            consisting of all pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y\in L
            ) such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(x)=j(y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\to L/E
            is a surjective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
          %p
            Vice versa, given a congruence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi E
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(x)=\bigvee_{y\colon (x,y)\in E}y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is the nucleus corresponding to the sublocale
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\to L/E
          %p
            Given a nucleus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\to j(L)
          %p
            Vice versa, given a surjective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+frames"} morphism of frames
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^*\colon L\to S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_* h^*\colon L\to L
            is a nucleus on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            Given a nucleus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\colon L\to L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(L)
            is a sublocale.
          %p
            Vice versa, given a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subset L
            that is a sublocale, the corresponding nucleus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\colon L\to L
            is given by the formula
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(a)=\bigwedge\{s\in S\mid a\le s\}
          %h2#special_cases Special cases
          %p
            Of course, every locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a sublocale of itself. The corresponding nucleus is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_L(U) \coloneqq U ,
          %p
            so every open is preserved in this sublocale. Conversely, every locale has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+subspace"} empty
            sublocale, given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi ∅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi L
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\empty(U) \coloneqq L .
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an open in the locale
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            defines an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspace"} open subspace
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_U(V) \coloneqq U \Rightarrow V ,
          %p
            so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_U(V)
            is the largest open which agrees with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            also defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'
            (or any other notation for a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{U'}(V) \coloneqq U \cup V ,
          %p
            so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{U'}(V)
            is the largest open which agrees with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            except on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is also topological; the same goes for closed sublocales, assuming
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
            in the lattice of sublocales.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+sublocale"} double negation sublocale
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\neg\neg}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ¬
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi U
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{\neg\neg}(U) \coloneqq \neg{\neg{U}} .
          %p
            This is always a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subspace"} dense subspace
            %em smallest
            dense sublocale of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is topological,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{\neg\neg}
            is rarely topological; in fact, its only points are the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isolated+point"} isolated point
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %h2#relation_to_topological_subspaces Relation to topological subspaces
          %p
            The underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            will typically have many sublocales that are not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spatial+locale"} spatial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            However, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be equipped with the induced topology, which turns it into a subspace, whose underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            is a sublocale of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms+of+frames"} morphisms of frames
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and an open subset of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Thus, we have a canonical map from the set of (topological) subspaces of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the set of spatial sublocales of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
          %p
            This map is injective if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            (VI.1.2 in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PicadoPultr12"} PP12
          %p
            This map is a surjection if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober space
            (Proposition VI.2.2.1 in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PicadoPultr12"} PP12
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , II.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+Spaces"} Stone Spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 3
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/logic-categories-and-sets/stone-spaces?format=PB&isbn=9780521337793"} ISBN:9780521337793
            %li#PicadoPultr12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Picado"}> Jorge Picado
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ales%CC%8C+Pultr"} Aleš Pultr
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frames+and+Locales"} Frames and Locales
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
